# Every deadline in the main sources, judged: tools/check/deadline-sites.py says what a site is and what each verdict
# means. <path> | <function> | <form> | <count> | <verdict> | <reason>. The question for each: what happens when the
# deadline fires as the bounded work returns (the timeout lands on another thread after the block returned and before
# the timeout's scope completed)? A new site, or one more in a function, fails until it is judged here. drops-result
# marks the sites whose caller acts on a result the deadline can drop: known faults, each to be fixed with a race test.
kuicksilver-bench/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/bench/MemoryBench.kt | endpointIdle | withTimeout | 2 | side-effect-free | harness bound: the timeout fails the run or the iteration, nothing of the library depends on the result
kuicksilver-http2/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http2/runtime/H2Runtime.kt | awaitAnswer | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | joins the stream's answered Deferred; the caller goes on either way, the answer stays in the stream
kuicksilver-http2/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http2/runtime/H2Runtime.kt | closeWithinBound | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | both branches end alike: a transport whose close completed as the bound fires is closed hard, and closeTransportOnce does nothing to a closed one
kuicksilver-http2/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http2/runtime/H2Runtime.kt | runHealthCheck | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | made-flag | a PING acknowledgement read as the bound fires is taken from acked.isCompleted, not from the dropped result (CHANGELOG: "a health PING answered as its bound fires keeps the connection")
kuicksilver-http2/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http2/runtime/H2Runtime.kt | timerLoop | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | the kick only wakes the loop, which reads the core's timers again on every turn; a kick dropped at the deadline is not needed
kuicksilver-http2/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http2/runtime/H2Runtime.kt | waitWithin | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | made-flag | moved is set as the wait returns: a window or written frame taken as the send-stall bound fires is progress, not a stall
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/H3Session.control.kt | readUni | timer | 1 | made-flag | the timer reads header.settled, which the reader sets when the type arrived; a header read as the timer fires is kept
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/H3Session.critical.kt | attemptUntilTheLimitIsLow | timer | 1 | completedWithin | the attempt stores its result before it returns, and the guard's cancel gives the stored result (the same store-before-return)
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/H3Session.kt | withinWtDeadline | select-cancel | 1 | completedWithin | the timer branch joins the cancelled block and returns its result when it completed all the same (CHANGELOG: "the WebTransport deadline keeps a CONNECT that completed after it was chosen")
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/H3Session.shutdown.kt | goAwayConfined | timer | 1 | made-flag | rejects only the heads still pending with the same reader; a head read meanwhile left pendingHeaders and is the application's
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/RequestStream.kt | handOver | select-cancel | 1 | side-effect-free | a flush cancelled because the transport closed: nothing is taken from anyone, and a flush that completed first is left as it is
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/ServerRequestStream.kt | readRequestStream | timer | 1 | made-flag | the head timer acts only while head.settled is false; the reader settles the head as it arrives, so a head read in time is kept
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/webtransport/WtSessionImpl.kt | endConnect | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | joins the capsule reader for the peer's FIN; peerFinished is read after the wait, not the dropped result (the writes use completedWithin since class-sweep)
